  "note": "Municipal election at Warrenpoint, May 1936. Only the West Ward went to the poll, for seven seats; the East Ward was filled without a contest. The contest turned on the question of mixed bathing at the municipal baths. The five East Ward members were returned unopposed (Irish News, 6 May 1936, p. 7; Newry Reporter, 7 May 1936, p. 5). Returned without a poll. Full names in the Newry Reporter: James D. Gordon (printed 'Cordon' there; 'Gordon' in the Irish News and the News-Letter), T. H. Greene, Robert Linden, James Savage, John Toombs. Returned unopposed."
